# NOMMA Issuing CA Signing Workflow

This file is generated by Ansible and copied to {{ admin_cert_dir }}.

## Files

- `nomma-issuing-ca.csr.pem`: Intermediate CA CSR.
- `nomma-issuing-ca.cert.pem`: Intermediate CA certificate signed by the offline Root CA.
- `nomma-ca-chain.cert.pem`: Intermediate + Root certificate chain.
- `nomma-root-ca.cert.pem`: Public Root CA certificate.
- `server-cert-openssl-example.cnf`: Example SAN CSR config for future server certificates.

## Root CA security rule

The Root CA private key stays only on the offline Root CA host:

`{{ root_ca_key_path }}`

Do not copy it to user folders, network shares, Git, ticket systems, or email.

## Validation

```bash
openssl verify -CAfile {{ root_ca_cert_path }} {{ intermediate_ca_cert_path }}
openssl x509 -in {{ intermediate_ca_cert_path }} -noout -text
```

